```cpp
TF_RETURN_IF_ERROR(c->WithRank(perm_shape, 1, &perm_shape));
TF_RETURN_IF_ERROR(c->WithValue(perm_elems, rank, &perm_elems));
```
- Ensures `perm_shape.rank() == 1` (verified)
- Ensures `perm->NumElements() == rank` (verified)

**Line 61-62: Type conversion (DANGEROUS POINT)**
```cpp
if (perm->dtype() == DT_INT32) {
  data = AsInt64<int32>(perm, rank);
} else {
  data = AsInt64<int64_t>(perm, rank);
}
```
- `AsInt64<T>(perm, rank)` reads `rank` elements from `perm` tensor into `std::vector<int64_t>`
- If `perm->dtype() == DT_INT32`, each `int32_t` value is converted to `int64_t`
- **No check if `int64_t` conversion overflows** the 32-bit source value

**Line 64-73: Index bounds check (TOO LATE)**
```cpp
for (int32_t i = 0; i < rank; ++i) {
  int64_t in_idx = data[i];
  if (in_idx >= rank || in_idx <= -rank) {
    return errors::InvalidArgument("perm dim ", in_idx,
                                   " is out of range of input rank ", rank);
  }
  dims[i] = c->Dim(input, in_idx);
}
```
- **Bounds check performed AFTER** `int64_t` conversion
- Fails only if final `int64_t` value is out of range
- Does NOT fail if `int64_t` value overflows from a larger `int32_t`

